Notes
=====

Get files in directory:
> $ find path/to/dir -type f -exec shasum -a 256 {} \; > x_library_checksums.txt

Filter out non-music:
> $ grep -vE '(Thumbs.db|\.png|\.ini|\.jpg|\.DS_Store|txt)$' x_library_checksums.txt > x_library_checksums_pruned.txt

Sort:
> $ sort x_library_checksums_pruned.txt > x.sorted

Get just the hashes
> $ cut -d ' ' -f1 x.sorted > x.hashes

> $ comm -23 source.hashes nas.hashes | wc -l

Get the lines from nas's checksums that match the checksums of source's songs:
> $ grep -F -f source.hashes nas.sorted > nas_from_source.txt
> $ sed -E 's/^([0-9a-zA-Z]{64})  /\1\t/' nas_from_source.txt > nas_from_source.map
> $ sed -E 's/^([0-9a-zA-Z]{64})  /\1\t/' source.sorted > source.map
> $ join -t $'\t' source.map nas_from_source.map > joined.txt

Find files that are in a different location on nas from on source computer:
awk -F '\t' '$2 != $3' joined.txt > moved_files.txt




Running the library snapshot/scan scripts
-----------------------------------------
On laptop:
```
    ./snapshot_source_music_library.py
    scp source_output.json nas:music_library_cleanup/
```
On nas:
```
    ./scan_library.py
```

To look at output:

* `jq . stale.json` look at info about files that may be out of date on the NAS (similar file has different hash on source)
* `jq .[].path exact.json` print NAS file paths for files that also exist on source
* `jq -r '.[] | "\(.path) -> \(.source_matches[0].source):\(.source_matches[0].path)"' stale.json` print paths on NAS and source library for files that are likely matches
